# Real key presses in the City bonds amount box: the number regroups as each digit lands, the
# caret stays beside the digit it was beside, and Backspace or Delete on a separator takes the
# digit next to it. Sells nothing.
name bond amount box: typing regroups, the caret keeps its digit, deleting skips separators
show-economy loans
bonds-section show
bonds-amount 500,000
# a 1 in front of 500,000
keys FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount home 1
expect-text-is FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 1,500,000
expect-caret FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 1
# Delete with the caret before the separator takes the 5
keys FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount delete
expect-text-is FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 100,000
expect-caret FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 1
# Backspace with the caret after a separator takes the digit before it
keys FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount end left left left backspace
expect-text-is FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 10,000
expect-caret FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 2
# typing in the middle
keys FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 7
expect-text-is FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 107,000
expect-caret FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 3
# backspacing the whole number never sticks on a separator
keys FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount end backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace backspace
expect-text-is FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount
keys FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 2 5 0 0 0 0 0
expect-text-is FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 2,500,000
expect-caret FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount 9
expect-text FinanceOverhaulBondsSell receive ₡2,500,000
cleanup:
blur FinanceOverhaulBondsAmount
bonds-amount 500,000
bonds-section auto
close-economy
